{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775208582,"nonce":"duSHD4P4saE9/gsBtEIJ9Jj1Qmg=","title":"Watcher does not exit promptly on Ctrl-C (SIGINT). The process hangs for 30+ seconds or requires a second Ctrl-C / kill.","message":"`TelegramRelay.poll_all()` in `host/watcher/telegram_relay.py` makes a blocking HTTP request:\n```python\nresp = _pkg().requests.get(\n    f\"https://api.telegram.org/bot{self.token}/getUpdates\",\n    params={\"offset\": self._offset, \"timeout\": TG_LONG_POLL_TIMEOUT_S},\n    timeout=TG_HTTP_TIMEOUT_S,\n)\n```\nThe main loop in `host_watcher.py:240` calls `poll_all()` synchronously. When Ctrl-C fires, the shutdown event is set but the loop is stuck waiting for the HTTP response (up to `TG_HTTP_TIMEOUT_S`). The shutdown check at line 235 only runs after `poll_all()` returns.\n\n**Fix:** Move Telegram polling to a separate thread (already has `_poll_thread` infrastructure but `poll_all` is called inline), or use `requests.Session` with a short timeout and retry loop that checks `_shutdown`.\n\n`host/watcher/tracker_writer.py:196` calls `self._pool.shutdown(wait=False)`. Connection handler threads blocked on `recv_json_line(conn)` (30s socket timeout) won't be joined. \n\n**Fix:** Set socket timeout to 1-2s on accepted connections, or use `shutdown(wait=True)` with a bounded timeout.\n\n`TrackerWriter.stop()` only waits 10s for the thread to finish. If the queue is full and the writer is processing slow tracker operations, the join times out and the thread keeps running.\n\n**Fix:** Increase join timeout or drain the queue before joining.\n\n`host/watcher/qa_handler.py:54` has `time.sleep(PRE_PAUSE_DELAY_S)` that doesn't check the shutdown event.\n\n**Fix:** Use `shutdown_event.wait(timeout=PRE_PAUSE_DELAY_S)` instead of `time.sleep()`.\n\n1. Start watcher: `nightshift watcher`\n2. Wait for at least one poll cycle\n3. Press Ctrl-C\n4. Observe: process does not exit for 30+ seconds\n\nWatcher exits within 1-2 seconds of Ctrl-C.\n\nREQ: REQ-019 (graceful shutdown)","files":null}]}